{"name":"Tavern Creek","hex":"#957046","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tavern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A restaurant or bar.","A building containing a bar licensed to sell alcoholic drinks, and offering sleeping accommodations for travelers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tavern"},{"term":"creek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small inlet, often saltwater, leading to the sea or to the main channel of a river, especially a river estuary.","The inner part of a port that is used as a dock for small boats."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/creek"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tavern Creek (Missouri River tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Tavern Creek is a stream in St. Louis, Franklin and St. Charles counties of east central Missouri. It is a tributary of the Fiddle Creek."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tavern_Creek_(Missouri_River_tributary)","wikidata":"Q27985054"},{"title":"Tavern Creek (Osage River tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Tavern Creek is a stream in Miller and Pulaski counties in the U.S. state of Missouri. It is a tributary of the Osage River. The stream headwaters are at 37°54′42″N 92°22′19″W and the confluence with the Osage is at 38°19′04″N 92°17′24″W."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tavern_Creek_(Osage_River_tributary)","wikidata":"Q27985722"},{"title":"Tavern","blocks":[{"text":"A tavern is a type of business where people gather to drink alcoholic beverages and be served food, such as different types of roast meats and cheese, and where travelers would receive lodging. An inn is a tavern that has a licence to put up guests as lodgers. The word derives from the Latin taberna whose original meaning was a shed, workshop, stall, or pub."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg/330px-Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbna